              "text": "You can download the latest version of Python directly from the official Python website:\n\n* **Official Downloads Page:** [python.org/downloads](https://www.python.org/downloads/)\n\n### How to Install on Your Operating System:\n\n* **Windows:** \n  You can download the standard Windows installer directly from the downloads page. When running the installer, **make sure to check the box that says \"Add Python.exe to PATH\"** before clicking install, as this allows you to run Python easily from your command prompt or terminal. Alternatively, you can install it via the Microsoft Store.\n  \n* **macOS:** \n  You can download the macOS installer (`.pkg` file) from the downloads page. Alternatively, if you use the [Homebrew](https://brew.sh/) package manager, you can install it through your terminal by running:\n  ```bash\n  brew install python\n  ```\n\n* **Linux / UNIX:** \n  Most Linux distributions come with Python pre-installed. To update to the latest version, it is highly recommended to use your system's package manager rather than downloading the installer from the website. For example:\n  * **Debian/Ubuntu:** `sudo apt update && sudo apt install python3`\n  * **Fedora:** `sudo dnf install python3`\n\n*After installing, you can verify that it is set up correctly by opening your terminal or command prompt and typing `python --version` or `python3 --version`.*",
